WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:01.968
Hello, I'm Camille.

2
00:00:02.318 --> 00:00:05.990
Today: fake investments, those deals that are too good to be true.

3
00:00:06.690 --> 00:00:11.610
It often starts with an ad on social media, featuring a well-known personality.

4
00:00:11.960 --> 00:00:15.664
Sometimes, the video is faked with artificial intelligence.

5
00:00:16.014 --> 00:00:21.998
You leave your details. A very friendly adviser calls you back, and offers you an exceptional investment.

6
00:00:22.698 --> 00:00:24.450
Here are the telltale signs.

7
00:00:24.800 --> 00:00:27.880
A high return, presented as guaranteed and risk-free.

8
00:00:28.230 --> 00:00:31.310
Pressure to invest quickly, and more and more.

9
00:00:31.660 --> 00:00:34.868
Gains shown on a website, but impossible to withdraw.

10
00:00:35.218 --> 00:00:38.730
And when you try to get your money back, new fees to pay.

11
00:00:39.430 --> 00:00:43.966
Remember the Crow and the Fox: every flatterer lives at the expense of those who listen.

12
00:00:44.316 --> 00:00:46.916
A return that's too good to be true… is false.

13
00:00:47.616 --> 00:00:49.976
Before investing, always check.

14
00:00:50.326 --> 00:00:56.110
Check the regulator: the FCA Warning List in the UK, or Investor.gov in the US.

15
00:00:56.460 --> 00:00:58.340
Ask your bank for advice.

16
00:00:58.690 --> 00:01:03.338
And if someone offers to recover your lost money for a fee, it's another scam.

17
00:01:04.038 --> 00:01:06.094
Distrust is the mother of safety.

18
00:01:06.444 --> 00:01:09.404
That was Camille, for Prometis. See you soon!
